{"id":"spiti-circuit","title":"Spiti Valley circuit","who":"Classic route · Kinnaur and Spiti by motorcycle or car","when":"June to October (Kunzum La open); September is best","vehicle":"Motorcycle or car, 8–12 days","kind":"moto","color":"#0d9488","summary":"A Himalayan loop from Shimla up the Sutlej gorge through Kinnaur, into the cold desert of Spiti with its cliff-top monasteries and villages above 4,000 m, then over the Kunzum La past Chandratal lake and down to Manali. Do it this way round for the altitude.","sources":[{"label":"Walk with Vicky: Chennai to Spiti (October 2025)","url":"https://walkwithvicky.blogspot.com/2025/10/chennai-to-spiti-ultimate-himalayan-adventure.html"},{"label":"Discover with Dheeraj: Kinnaur–Spiti circuit itinerary","url":"https://discoverwithdheeraj.com/kinnaur-spiti-circuit-itinerary-2026/"},{"label":"Travel Coffee: Spiti Valley road status (May 2026)","url":"https://travelcoffee.in/blog/spiti-valley-road-status"}],"approximate":"The common clockwise loop and overnight villages.","km":746,"bbox":[77.1285,31.086,78.6392,32.4512],"stops":[{"name":"Shimla","place":"Shimla, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.104,77.1708],"text":"The old British summer capital, the start.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Landscape_of_Shimla_%2C_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg/500px-Landscape_of_Shimla_%2C_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg","page":"Shimla","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landscape_of_Shimla_%2C_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg","credit":"Navneet Sharma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Narkanda","place":"Narkanda, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.2548,77.4613],"text":"Apple country on a ridge with the first snow peaks in view.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/NARKANDA.jpg/500px-NARKANDA.jpg","page":"Narkanda","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NARKANDA.jpg","credit":"Manjeet44877","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Sangla","place":"Sangla, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.3118,78.5381],"text":"Up the Sutlej into Kinnaur and the Baspa valley."},{"name":"Chitkul","place":"Chitkul, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.3518,78.4359],"text":"Wooden houses in the last village before Tibet.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Temple_at_Chitkul.JPG/500px-Temple_at_Chitkul.JPG","page":"Chitkul","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_at_Chitkul.JPG","credit":"Kaiho","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kalpa","place":"Kalpa, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.5778,78.2286],"text":"Facing the Kinnaur Kailash range."},{"name":"Nako","place":"Nako, Himachal Pradesh","at":[31.8814,78.627],"text":"Past cliff roads like the one at Malling to a lake village near the Tibet border.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Nako_Village.jpg/500px-Nako_Village.jpg","page":"Nako, Himachal Pradesh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nako_Village.jpg","credit":"Sumita Roy Dutta","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tabo","place":"Tabo, Himachal Pradesh","at":[32.094,78.3837],"text":"A monastery more than a thousand years old, with its painted halls.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Tabo_Monjastery_Entrance.jpg/500px-Tabo_Monjastery_Entrance.jpg","page":"Tabo Monastery","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tabo_Monjastery_Entrance.jpg","credit":"Arup1981","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Dhankar","place":"Dhankar, Himachal Pradesh","at":[32.0906,78.2149],"text":"A fort-monastery on a crumbling ridge above two rivers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Dhankar_Gompa_and_village.jpg/500px-Dhankar_Gompa_and_village.jpg","page":"Dhankar Gompa","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhankar_Gompa_and_village.jpg","credit":"John Hill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Kaza","place":"Kaza, Himachal Pradesh","at":[32.2244,78.0723],"text":"Spiti's small capital, base for Key monastery, Kibber, Langza and Komic.","source":{"label":"Walk with Vicky (2025)","url":"https://walkwithvicky.blogspot.com/2025/10/chennai-to-spiti-ultimate-himalayan-adventure.html"}},{"name":"Losar","place":"Losar, Himachal Pradesh","at":[32.4382,77.7501],"text":"The last Spiti village before the pass."},{"name":"Chandratal","place":"Chandratal","at":[32.4753,77.6175],"text":"Over the Kunzum La to the \"moon lake\" at 4,300 m. Camps nearby; best after time at altitude.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Chandratal_1.JPG/500px-Chandratal_1.JPG","page":"Chandra Taal","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandratal_1.JPG","credit":"Lodhra","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Manali","place":"Manali, Himachal Pradesh","at":[32.2455,77.1873],"text":"Rough road through Batal and Chhatru, then the Atal Tunnel down to Manali.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Manali_City.jpg/500px-Manali_City.jpg","page":"Manali, Himachal Pradesh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manali_City.jpg","credit":"Neerajsinghazm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":61,"line":[[31.1041,77.1707],[31.1195,77.2365],[31.086,77.3009],[31.1276,77.3406],[31.118,77.3748],[31.1395,77.3871],[31.1924,77.3795],[31.2187,77.4124],[31.2022,77.4214],[31.2217,77.436],[31.2404,77.427],[31.2546,77.4611]]},{"by":"ride","km":193,"line":[[31.2546,77.4611],[31.2543,77.5004],[31.3227,77.4906],[31.3291,77.5243],[31.3283,77.5044],[31.3411,77.5263],[31.3357,77.5067],[31.3529,77.4868],[31.3495,77.5241],[31.3888,77.5544],[31.3887,77.6289],[31.4503,77.6309],[31.4603,77.6728],[31.502,77.714],[31.5261,77.7811],[31.5423,77.7851],[31.5426,77.8147],[31.5742,77.8521],[31.5546,77.8821],[31.5672,77.8878],[31.5519,77.9144],[31.5662,77.9301],[31.562,77.9896],[31.5252,78.0542],[31.5116,78.1682],[31.4692,78.1857],[31.4402,78.2227],[31.401,78.3448],[31.3524,78.4123],[31.3411,78.493],[31.3023,78.5319]]},{"by":"r